<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    nexus-nyry9.9 (RDR-196 Phase 1 Step 3, ENGINE HALF) — nx_answer_steps:
    per-step cost/quality telemetry, one row per EXECUTED dispatch segment
    (nexus-nyry9.8's StepRecord, src/nexus/plans/runner.py:242). Child of
    nx_answer_runs (telemetry-001-baseline.xml, changesets telemetry-001-7/8)
    — NOT an edit of that shipped changeset (a checksum break); this is a
    NEW file at the changelog TAIL, matching the established late-append
    convention (D0.1; see telemetry-004's / telemetry-006's own <include>
    comments for the identical reasoning).

    Column list is the FROZEN shape from nexus-nyry9.8's critique (T2
    nexus/review-nexus-nyry9.8 [23057]), matching StepRecord field-for-field:
    run_id, step_index, operator, source, model, input_tokens, output_tokens,
    cost_usd, elapsed_ms, ok, bundled_steps — plus tenant_id + RLS, exactly
    like the parent.

    PRIMARY KEY (run_id, step_index): a fused bundle (StepRecord's own
    docstring, runner.py:246-252) is ONE dispatch segment that may cover
    several plan-step indices, but it still produces exactly ONE step
    record, filed at its first fused index — so (run_id, step_index) stays
    a true 1:1 key against the rows this table ever receives; the full set
    of covered indices lives in bundled_steps, not in extra PK-conflicting
    rows. No surrogate id column: unlike nx_answer_runs (an independently
    queried top-level event log with its own ETL dedup key), a step row is
    only ever reached through its run, so the composite PK is both the
    natural key AND the access path (a leading-run_id btree scan), with no
    second identity to carry.

    FK run_id -> nexus.nx_answer_runs(id) ON DELETE CASCADE: a step row has
    no independent existence once its run is gone (deleting a run's event
    record should not orphan its children), and RDR-080's own retention
    story is run-level, never per-step.

    source CHECK ('llm','sql','bundle'): the closed three-value set
    StepRecord.source's own docstring (runner.py:274-282) already commits
    to — no fourth value invented, enforced here rather than left to
    convention alone.

    cost_usd NUMERIC (not DOUBLE PRECISION): chosen correctly from this
    column's first day, per the column-type-discipline note on this bead
    (nexus-cefa1 arc precedent — money is not a float). This is a
    DELIBERATE divergence from the parent nx_answer_runs.cost_usd, which
    stays DOUBLE PRECISION (telemetry-001-baseline.xml:194) in this
    changeset. Retyping the parent to numeric was evaluated and explicitly
    NOT done here: NX_ANSWER_RUNS.COST_USD is a jOOQ-generated field read
    and written at import/live-write/aggregate/row-mapper call sites
    throughout TelemetryRepository.java and TelemetryHandler.java (e.g.
    the avg(NX_ANSWER_RUNS.COST_USD) aggregate, the row mapper, the ETL
    import path) — retyping it flips the generated Java type from Double
    to BigDecimal at every one of those existing, unrelated call sites and
    risks a wire-shape change in already-shipped JSON responses (BigDecimal
    serializes differently than Double). That is real, separable work in
    the shape of telemetry-004-type-hygiene.xml's own dedicated retype
    pass, not a rider on a new-table bead whose own column gets the right
    type from birth. Recorded here per this bead's own instruction: "if you
    find a reason not to (readers that depend on float), document the
    divergence in the changeset comment and the handback instead."

    bundled_steps INTEGER[] NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}': the full set of 0-based
    plan indices a source='bundle' record fused; empty for every other
    source (StepRecord.bundled_steps docstring, runner.py:275-278).

    input_tokens / output_tokens / cost_usd all NULLABLE: mirrors
    StepRecord's own `| None` widening (runner.py:283-300) — a "sql" step
    is a true, known zero (never written as NULL by the client; the
    column itself still permits NULL because nothing at the schema layer
    can distinguish "this bead's Python caller always fills 0" from a
    future caller that has a genuine unknown-cost case, and the RDR's own
    risk register treats "absent fields record None, never 0.0" as
    binding). model NULLABLE for the same "None is the only absent
    spelling" reason (StepRecord.model docstring, runner.py:263-272).

    No updated_at / no UpdatedAtTrigger: matches the parent nx_answer_runs
    exactly — this is an append-only event-log record engine-side (a step
    is recorded once, at run-completion time, and never mutated in place),
    the same shape as every other telemetry-001 event-log table.

    No ETL dedup unique index: unlike the top-level event logs
    (relevance_log, tier_writes, nx_answer_runs, hook_failures), a step
    row has no independent ETL import path in this bead's scope — the
    live-write POST /v1/telemetry/nx_answer_runs/record path is the only
    writer (see TelemetryHandler.java's handleNxAnswerRunRecord), and it
    is idempotent via the PARENT's own onConflictDoNothing() (a skipped
    parent insert also skips its children — see recordNxAnswerRun's own
    javadoc). A dedicated importNxAnswerStepRow ETL path is out of this
    bead's scope (not requested by nexus-nyry9.9's DO list) and would earn
    its own dedup index if it is ever added.

    Grants: no explicit GRANT statement in this file. grants-nexus-svc.xml
    (included immediately after this file, D0.1 tail placement) is a
    runAlways block that walks every table currently in the nexus schema
    and grants SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE to nexus_svc dynamically (plus
    ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES for future tables) — this table is picked up
    by that sweep automatically, the same way every telemetry-00N table
    since telemetry-001 has been.

    Placement: changelog TAIL, immediately after telemetry-006-frecency-
    ttl-null.xml (the current tail, nexus-tk070.p6b) and before the
    grants-nexus-svc.xml runAlways block — the established late-append
    convention (D0.1) every new changeset since RDR-156 follows.

    ── telemetry-007-3 (RDR-196 .p1c-b, nexus-lme1s) ─────────────────────

    nx_answer_runs.cost_usd DROP NOT NULL + DROP DEFAULT: appended to this
    SAME file rather than a new tail file — telemetry-007 has not shipped
    in any engine-service tag yet (verified via a git tag containment
    check against its landing commit before this changeset was authored),
    so appending is the D0.1-compliant move, not a checksum-breaking edit
    of a shipped changeset.

    Risk 1 (RDR-196, "zeros are not free"): the client (nexus-nyry9.10,
    src/nexus/mcp/core.py) now sends a JSON `cost_usd: null` on the parent
    run row when NO usage was observed at all (as opposed to a genuine
    known-zero, e.g. a pure-T3 fast-path call) — see that bead's dev notes
    for the full "ENGINE LIMITATION FOUND" writeup: prior to this
    changeset, `NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.0` forced that null into a stored 0.0,
    indistinguishable from "this call was free." NUMERIC/DOUBLE PRECISION
    stays DOUBLE PRECISION here — the type-hygiene divergence from the
    child `nx_answer_steps.cost_usd` (NUMERIC) is unchanged and was already
    decided + documented at telemetry-007-1 above; this changeset only
    lifts the NOT NULL/DEFAULT constraint, it does not retype the column.

    Readers updated in lockstep (same commit as this changeset, not a
    follow-up): `TelemetryRepository.queryNxAnswerRuns`'s
    `avg(NX_ANSWER_RUNS.COST_USD)` aggregate already ignores NULLs per
    standard SQL AVG semantics (asserted by a new repository test, not
    just assumed); the row mapper emits the raw (possibly-null) value,
    which Jackson serializes as JSON `null`, never a fabricated `0`; the
    live-write path (`recordNxAnswerRun`) and the fidelity-preserving ETL
    import path (`importNxAnswerRunRow`) both now accept a `Double`
    (boxed, nullable) `costUsd` parameter instead of a primitive `double`
    that could never carry "absent" as anything but 0.0.

    Rollback: COALESCEs any existing NULLs to 0.0 before restoring
    `NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.0` — a rollback must never fail on data this
    changeset itself could have legitimately written (the "legacy-cleanup
    migrations never wedge a user upgrade" doctrine, applied here to a
    forward-then-back cycle rather than a legacy cleanup, because the
    failure shape is identical: a NOT NULL restore over live NULLs must
    not abort).
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <!-- ── Changeset telemetry-007-1: nx_answer_steps ──────────────────────── -->
    <changeSet id="telemetry-007-1" author="nexus-nyry9.9">
        <comment>Create nx_answer_steps table (event log; RDR-196 per-step cost/quality telemetry)</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
CREATE TABLE nexus.nx_answer_steps (
    run_id        BIGINT       NOT NULL REFERENCES nexus.nx_answer_runs(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    tenant_id     TEXT         NOT NULL,
    step_index    INTEGER      NOT NULL,
    operator      TEXT         NOT NULL,
    source        TEXT         NOT NULL,
    model         TEXT,
    input_tokens  INTEGER,
    output_tokens INTEGER,
    cost_usd      NUMERIC,
    elapsed_ms    INTEGER      NOT NULL,
    ok            BOOLEAN      NOT NULL,
    bundled_steps INTEGER[]    NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',
    CONSTRAINT nx_answer_steps_pk PRIMARY KEY (run_id, step_index),
    CONSTRAINT nx_answer_steps_source_chk CHECK (source IN ('llm', 'sql', 'bundle'))
);
        </sql>
        <rollback>DROP TABLE IF EXISTS nexus.nx_answer_steps CASCADE</rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- ── Changeset telemetry-007-2: nx_answer_steps RLS ──────────────────── -->
    <changeSet id="telemetry-007-2" author="nexus-nyry9.9">
        <comment>RLS: ENABLE + FORCE + tenant_isolation policy on nx_answer_steps</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.nx_answer_steps ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE nexus.nx_answer_steps FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY tenant_isolation ON nexus.nx_answer_steps
    USING      (tenant_id = current_setting('nexus.tenant', true))
    WITH CHECK (tenant_id = current_setting('nexus.tenant', true));
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            DROP POLICY IF EXISTS tenant_isolation ON nexus.nx_answer_steps;
            ALTER TABLE nexus.nx_answer_steps NO FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
            ALTER TABLE nexus.nx_answer_steps DISABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- ── Changeset telemetry-007-3: nx_answer_runs.cost_usd nullable ─────── -->
    <changeSet id="telemetry-007-3" author="nexus-lme1s">
        <comment>nx_answer_runs.cost_usd: DROP NOT NULL + DROP DEFAULT — a client "no usage observed" null must not land as a stored 0.0 (RDR-196 risk 1)</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.nx_answer_runs ALTER COLUMN cost_usd DROP NOT NULL;
ALTER TABLE nexus.nx_answer_runs ALTER COLUMN cost_usd DROP DEFAULT;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
UPDATE nexus.nx_answer_runs SET cost_usd = 0.0 WHERE cost_usd IS NULL;
ALTER TABLE nexus.nx_answer_runs ALTER COLUMN cost_usd SET DEFAULT 0.0;
ALTER TABLE nexus.nx_answer_runs ALTER COLUMN cost_usd SET NOT NULL;
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
